<!--
  modules/scinotes/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 5 module POM (Wave E, the FINAL
  wave) (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/scinotes -am package from
  the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/scinotes/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/scinotes/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build;
  nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Wave E is the last wave — scinotes, preferences, xcos —
  and completes the 23-module reactor. scinotes (140 source files) is listed
  first of the three because preferences imports scinotes directly (see
  modules/preferences/pom.xml), so scinotes must exist in the reactor before
  preferences can depend on it; xcos also depends on scinotes' siblings core/
  graph/gui/helptools/javasci/types but not on scinotes itself.

  A TOOL BUG, FOUND HERE, THAT AFFECTS ALL THREE MODULES' RAW OUTPUT. On this
  platform (macOS, BSD sed), maven-module-deps.sh's section [1] pipeline
  strips "import " via `sed -E 's/^\s*import\s+(static\s+)?//'` — but BSD
  sed's -E (POSIX ERE) does NOT support the `\s` GNU shorthand at all, so
  that substitution is a silent no-op: every section-[1] line keeps its
  literal "import " prefix. The self-package exclusion one step later
  (`grep -vE "^org\.scilab\.(modules|forge)\.$MOD(\.|$)"`) is anchored on
  `^org\.`, which can never match a line still starting with "import ", so it
  never fires either — a module's OWN sub-packages leak into its own
  "reactor imports" list instead of being excluded. Confirmed directly:
  `echo "org.scilab.modules.scinotes.actions" | grep -vE "^org\.scilab\.
  (modules|forge)\.scinotes(\.|$)"` exits 1 (correctly excluded) in
  isolation, but running the SCRIPT's actual multi-stage pipeline over
  scinotes' real source left "import org.scilab.modules.scinotes",
  "...scinotes.actions", "...scinotes.tabfactory", "...scinotes.utils" sitting
  unfiltered in section [1]'s output — self-references to scinotes' own
  packages, not reactor dependencies. Reproduced with POSIX bracket classes
  (`[[:space:]]` instead of `\s`, functionally identical, portable to BSD
  sed) to get a corrected list; every dependency below was cross-checked
  against that corrected, self-reference-free pass, not the raw script
  output alone. This is a pre-existing latent bug in the tool itself (not
  touched here — out of this task's scope, and every earlier wave's own POMs
  were seemingly written by a reader who recognized and mentally filtered the
  same self-referencing noise rather than by a tool that suppressed it), not
  a new one introduced this wave — flagged here once, for whoever next reads
  a maven-module-deps.sh transcript against a large multi-package module on
  macOS. modules/preferences/pom.xml and modules/xcos/pom.xml cross-reference
  this paragraph rather than repeating it.

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh scinotes, 140 files; self-reference
  noise removed per the paragraph above):
    [1] imports resolve to TEN reactor dependencies, all below (all already
        migrated by earlier waves):
          action_binding ({,highlevel.}InterpreterManagement /
          ScilabInterpreterManagement — not actually imported by name here,
          see [3]), commons ({,filemonitor,gui,xml}.* plus a static import of
          commons.xml.XConfiguration), completion (AbstractSciCompletionWindow,
          Completion), console (AdvCLIManagement, CompletionAction,
          SciCompletionManager, SciInputParsingManager, SciPromptView,
          utils.ScilabLaTeXViewer), core (Scilab — SciNotes.java,
          SciNotesAutosave.java, a REAL import; core is Wave D, already
          migrated, so unlike modules/gui/pom.xml's reflection-only finding
          for the same class one wave earlier, scinotes reaches it directly),
          gui (bridge.{checkboxmenuitem,filechooser,menu,menubar,menuitem,
          tab,textbox,toolbar,window} plus a wide top-level surface —
          checkboxmenuitem, console, events.callback, filechooser, menu,
          menubar, menuitem, messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, tab,
          tabfactory, textbox, toolbar, utils), helptools (scilab.
          {AbstractScilabCodeHandler, HTMLWithStyleScilabCodeHandler,
          ScilabLexer} — confirmed present at modules/helptools/src/java/org/
          scilab/modules/helptools/scilab/), history_manager
          (HistoryManagement), jvm (LoadClassPath), localization (Messages).
    [2] reflection targets — NONE (the tool's own verdict: no forName/
        loadClass call anywhere in this module, inline or via a named
        constant). Independently re-confirmed with a direct `grep -rn
        'Class\.forName\|loadClass('` sweep of all 140 files: zero hits.
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import — every org.scilab.modules.*
        name is already covered by the ten reactor dependencies above
        (action_binding.{InterpreterManagement, highlevel.
        ScilabInterpreterManagement} included — used, just never imported by
        simple name), nothing new. The vendored-jar entries in this category
        (com.artenum.rosetta.*, org.apache.fop.apps.*,
        org.flexdock.docking.event.DockingEvent, javax.annotation.Generated)
        are handled below, each verified per-class or per-file, not merely
        copied from the tool's list.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  THE FOP / XMLGRAPHICS-COMMONS PAIR — utils/CodeExporter.java imports
  org.apache.fop.apps.{FOUserAgent, Fop, FopFactory, MimeConstants} and calls
  FopFactory.newInstance/newFOUserAgent/newFop plus reads
  MimeConstants.{MIME_PDF, MIME_POSTSCRIPT, MIME_EPS, MIME_RTF, MIME_PNG,
  MIME_FOP_AWT_PREVIEW, MIME_FOP_PRINT} — the SAME shape as modules/helptools/
  pom.xml's FopConverter.java, including the SAME inherited-superinterface
  trap that module's "ITERATION 1" comment documents in full: line 61 here,
  `MimeConstants.MIME_POSTSCRIPT`, is a constant javap confirms is declared
  on org.apache.xmlgraphics.util.MimeConstants (xmlgraphics-commons), not on
  fop-core's own org.apache.fop.apps.MimeConstants subinterface — resolving
  it needs the superinterface's class file at compile time even though
  scinotes' source never spells org.apache.xmlgraphics.* out directly.
  Applied here BEFORE a build iteration had to rediscover it (cross-
  referenced, not restated): both org.apache.xmlgraphics:fop-core:2.9 and
  org.apache.xmlgraphics:xmlgraphics-commons:2.9 below, same coordinates,
  same thirdparty/ files, same groupId as modules/helptools/pom.xml. Only
  the plain FOP/xmlgraphics-commons pair is needed — CodeExporter.java never
  touches org.scilab.forge.jlatexmath{,.fop}, net.sourceforge.jeuclid, or the
  freehep/avalon-framework jars that are FOP's OWN runtime implementation
  dependencies, not anything this module's source references (same
  "transitive runtime support, not this module's own compile need"
  reasoning as modules/gui/pom.xml's cc.sosonline.gpu finding).

  JAVAX.ANNOTATION-API — FOUR JFlex-generated lexers/scanners (ScilabLexer.
  java, FunctionScanner.java, IndentScanner.java, MatchingBlockScanner.java)
  each carry `@javax.annotation.Generated("JFlex")`, the exact same pattern
  modules/helptools/pom.xml and modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml already
  documented. Same jar, same coordinate (cross-referenced, not restated).

  THE TWO ROSETTA JARS, VERIFIED PER-CLASS, PLUS ONE SILENT-CLASS FINDING.
  utils/SciNotesCompletionWindow.java and actions/SciNotesCompletionAction.
  java directly import com.artenum.rosetta.core.CompletionItemImpl (engine)
  and com.artenum.rosetta.interfaces.{core,ui}.* (API) — `unzip -l` on both
  jars confirms every one of the eleven distinct classes this module's
  source names resolves across exactly jrosetta-API-1.0.4.jar (the nine
  interfaces.{core,ui}.* names) and jrosetta-engine-1.0.4.jar
  (CompletionItemImpl), same two coordinates as modules/console/pom.xml and
  modules/gui/pom.xml. THE SILENT CLASS: actions/SciNotesCompletionAction.
  java's own top-level class `extends org.scilab.modules.console.
  CompletionAction`, and console's CompletionAction (modules/console/src/
  java/org/scilab/modules/console/CompletionAction.java:35) in turn `extends
  com.artenum.rosetta.core.action.AbstractConsoleAction` — a THIRD rosetta
  package, com.artenum.rosetta.core.action, that appears ZERO times as text
  anywhere in scinotes' own source (confirmed: `grep -rn
  "rosetta.core.action" modules/scinotes/src/java` finds nothing) and that
  the tool's own scan therefore cannot report at all — the same class of gap
  its header names for helptools' inherited MimeConstants member, reached
  here through an EXTENDS chain instead of an inherited interface constant.
  `unzip -l thirdparty/jrosetta-engine-1.0.4.jar` confirms
  com/artenum/rosetta/core/action/AbstractConsoleAction.class lives there
  (not in jrosetta-API) — already covered by the jrosetta-engine dependency
  this module needs anyway for CompletionItemImpl, so no THIRD rosetta jar
  is required, but the finding is recorded here because the two jars being
  "already needed anyway" was confirmed, not assumed. The same file's two
  inner classes (SciNotesInputParsingManager extends console's
  SciInputParsingManager, SciNotesCompletionManager extends console's
  SciCompletionManager) were checked the same way — both superclasses'
  import lists resolve entirely to completion/localization (reactor
  siblings) and rosetta interfaces/core already accounted for above, nothing
  further.

  FLEXDOCK — org.flexdock.docking.event.DockingEvent, implemented by
  SciNotes.java, utils/NavigatorWindow.java and utils/SearchFile.java's
  DockingListener callbacks. SAME MECHANISM, SAME COORDINATE AS
  modules/commons/pom.xml and modules/gui/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not
  restated).
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>scinotes</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:19 <property name="library.title" value="Text editor for Scilab"/> -->
  <name>Text editor for Scilab</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.action_binding.{InterpreterManagement,
         highlevel.ScilabInterpreterManagement} — used unqualified across
         several actions classes (imported, not merely fully-qualified). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>action_binding</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.{CommonFileUtils, OS, ScilabCommons,
         ScilabCommonsUtils, ScilabConstants, ScilabGeneralPrefs,
         filemonitor.FileSystemMonitor, gui.*, xml.*}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.completion.{AbstractSciCompletionWindow,
         Completion} — utils/SciNotesCompletionWindow.java,
         actions/SciNotesCompletionAction.java. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>completion</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.console.{AdvCLIManagement, CompletionAction,
         SciCompletionManager, SciInputParsingManager, SciPromptView,
         utils.ScilabLaTeXViewer} — see this file's header comment, "THE TWO
         ROSETTA JARS... SILENT CLASS FINDING", for the extends chain this
         dependency's CompletionAction/SciCompletionManager/
         SciInputParsingManager classes sit at the root of. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>console</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.core.Scilab — SciNotes.java, SciNotesAutosave.
         java. A genuine compile-time import (core is Wave D, migrated the
         wave before this one) — contrast modules/gui/pom.xml's reflection-
         only finding for the identical class name one wave earlier, back
         when core was not yet migrated. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>core</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.* — this module's widest reactor surface:
         bridge.{checkboxmenuitem,filechooser,menu,menubar,menuitem,tab,
         textbox,toolbar,window} plus checkboxmenuitem, console,
         events.callback, filechooser, menu, menubar, menuitem,
         messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, tab, tabfactory, textbox, toolbar,
         utils. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.helptools.scilab.{AbstractScilabCodeHandler,
         HTMLWithStyleScilabCodeHandler, ScilabLexer} — utils/CodeExporter.
         java's HTML export path. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>helptools</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.history_manager.HistoryManagement. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>history_manager</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.jvm.LoadClassPath. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>jvm</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — the ordinary
         reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- THE TWO VENDORED ROSETTA JARS — SAME MECHANISM, SAME TWO
         COORDINATES AS modules/console/pom.xml and modules/gui/pom.xml (see
         this file's header comment for the per-class verification and the
         AbstractConsoleAction silent-class finding). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.artenum.rosetta</groupId>
      <artifactId>jrosetta-API</artifactId>
      <version>1.0.4</version>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>com.artenum.rosetta</groupId>
      <artifactId>jrosetta-engine</artifactId>
      <version>1.0.4</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- FOP-CORE — org.apache.fop.apps.{FOUserAgent, Fop, FopFactory,
         MimeConstants}, utils/CodeExporter.java's PDF/PS/EPS/RTF/PNG export
         engine. SAME COORDINATE AS modules/helptools/pom.xml (cross-
         referenced, not restated — see this file's header comment). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>fop-core</artifactId>
      <version>2.10</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- NOT DIRECTLY IMPORTED — needed for the identical inherited-
         superinterface reason modules/helptools/pom.xml documents in full
         ("ITERATION 1"): CodeExporter.java:61 reads
         MimeConstants.MIME_POSTSCRIPT, a constant declared on
         xmlgraphics-commons' org.apache.xmlgraphics.util.MimeConstants
         superinterface, not on fop-core's own subinterface. See this file's
         header comment, "THE FOP / XMLGRAPHICS-COMMONS PAIR". -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.apache.xmlgraphics</groupId>
      <artifactId>xmlgraphics-commons</artifactId>
      <version>2.9</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- javax.annotation.Generated("JFlex") on four generated lexers/
         scanners. Same jar, same coordinate as modules/helptools/pom.xml
         and modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml (cross-referenced, not
         restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>javax.annotation</groupId>
      <artifactId>javax.annotation-api</artifactId>
      <version>1.3.2</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- FLEXDOCK — org.flexdock.docking.event.DockingEvent (SciNotes.java,
         utils/NavigatorWindow.java, utils/SearchFile.java). SAME MECHANISM,
         SAME COORDINATE AS modules/commons/pom.xml and modules/gui/pom.xml
         (cross-referenced, not restated). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.flexdock</groupId>
      <artifactId>flexdock</artifactId>
      <version>1.2.5</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/scinotes/jar/org.scilab.modules.scinotes.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carried (now un-mangled to "è" by register P1) the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Implementation-Version is
                 present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000", positioned
                 between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor
                 exactly where Ant places it (Ant's live value there today:
                 "20260719 1729", a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair). -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
